  ],
  "description": "The low-level request(endpoint, payload, state_changing, expect) call as built before sending. input.payload is the ordered list of [key, value] pairs. The endpoint is trimmed of whitespace and slashes and must then be ASCII letters only (else {\"error\": \"ConfigurationError\"}); the names PlaceOrder, PlaceMultiOrder, ModifyOrder, CancelOrder, ExitSNOOrder, GenAcsTok, PlaceGTTOrder, ModifyGTTOrder, CancelGTTOrder, PlaceOCOOrder, ModifyOCOOrder, CancelOCOOrder, PlaceIceBergOrder, ModifyIceBergOrder, CancelIceBergOrder, GetQuotes, GetQuotesMultiple and TPSeries match case-insensitively and are rewritten to that spelling, every other name is sent as given. expected.state_changing is the caller's flag or a state-changing name; expected.rate_group is place_order (the orders group), quotes, tpseries or null; allow_empty is always false; expected.success_stats is the sorted list of success words (['Ok'] except the GTT, OCO and iceberg writes; the GTT and OCO words compare ignoring letter case, see success_words.json) and expected.requires_ack_id the field a success must carry as a non-blank string (al_id for the GTT and OCO writes, else null). Values may be nested objects and lists (the OCO bodies): their key and item order is kept, encoded as in jdata_encoding.json. uid is appended when absent; values become wire strings (true / false as Yes / No); a null value is {\"error\": \"TypeError\"} (a programming error, nothing is sent).",
  "source": "tradesmart._client_core.build_raw_call",
  "tolerance": {}
}
